cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use jobd in your work, please cite it as below."
title: jobd
abstract: >-
  A self-hostable, GPU-aware job broker for personal and lab-scale compute.
  jobd queues long-running batch work across heterogeneous machines, matching
  jobs to workers by capability tags (CUDA, VRAM capacity, installed tooling),
  and exposes the queue natively to language-model agents through the Model
  Context Protocol (MCP) in addition to a CLI and HTTP API. Designed for
  research workflows where compute outlives any single interactive session.
